# Rust Coding Standard

Read
[`.agents/skills/rust-coding-standard/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/rust-coding-standard/SKILL.md)
before you write or change any Rust code in this repository, and follow it.

The skill covers:

- Style: formatting, file size, comments, documentation, and naming.
- Design: the five SOLID principles (single responsibility, open/closed,
  Liskov substitution, interface segregation, dependency inversion) applied to
  traits, modules, and dependency direction.
- Idioms and robustness: ownership, error handling and exit codes, async, and
  tests.

The build already enforces formatting (`rustfmt.toml`) and lints (`Cargo.toml`,
`clippy.toml`). Do not edit those files to make code pass.
